# Theme JS + Alpine.js Patterns

**Owner:** loom
**Purpose:** Theme interactivity using vanilla JS first, Alpine.js for declarative state. NO jQuery, NO React.

## File Organization

```
assets/
  theme.js           # main entry, top-level event handlers
  cart-drawer.js     # cart drawer state + AJAX
  predictive-search.js  # search overlay
  product-form.js    # variant selector + add to cart
  alpine.min.js      # Alpine 3.x CDN copy
```

Load via theme.liquid:
```liquid
<script src="{{ 'alpine.min.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'cart-drawer.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
```

## Cart AJAX Pattern

```js
async function addToCart(variantId, quantity = 1) {
  const res = await fetch('/cart/add.js', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ id: variantId, quantity })
  });
  if (!res.ok) {
    document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:error', { detail: await res.json() }));
    return;
  }
  const item = await res.json();
  document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:added', { detail: item }));
  await refreshCartUI();
}

async function refreshCartUI() {
  const res = await fetch('/?section_id=cart-drawer');
  const html = await res.text();
  const parsed = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');
  const updated = parsed.querySelector('#cart-drawer');
  document.querySelector('#cart-drawer').replaceWith(updated);
}
```

Always use Section Rendering API (`?section_id=`) for cart updates — never regenerate cart HTML in JS.

## Alpine.js for Declarative UI

```html
<div x-data="{ open: false }" class="accordion">
  <button @click="open = !open" :aria-expanded="open">
    Frequently Asked Questions
  </button>
  <div x-show="open" x-collapse>
    <p>Content here</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

Use Alpine for: accordions, tabs, dropdowns, modals, tooltips, simple state. NOT for: cart logic, AJAX (use vanilla JS).

## Predictive Search

```js
const input = document.querySelector('#search-input');
let debounceTimer;
input.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
  clearTimeout(debounceTimer);
  debounceTimer = setTimeout(async () => {
    const q = e.target.value;
    if (q.length < 2) return;
    const res = await fetch(`/search/suggest.json?q=${encodeURIComponent(q)}&resources[type]=product`);
    const data = await res.json();
    renderSuggestions(data.resources.results.products);
  }, 200);
});
```

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ NO jQuery — vanilla JS or Alpine
- ❌ NO inline `<script>` in section files
- ❌ NO synchronous fetches
- ❌ NO `innerHTML` from user input (XSS — use `textContent` or templates)
- ❌ NO direct DOM manipulation when Alpine handles state better

<!-- AUTHORING TODO: Capture cart drawer, mega-menu, mobile nav, predictive search, sticky ATC patterns after first 3 projects. -->

# Online Store 2.0 JSON Templates

**Owner:** loom
**Purpose:** Build dynamic JSON templates so merchants can rearrange sections per page in customizer.

## Template Files

```
templates/
  index.json         # Home page
  product.json       # Default PDP
  product.{handle}.json  # Specific product PDP override
  collection.json    # Default collection
  collection.{handle}.json
  page.json          # Default page
  page.{handle}.json
  blog.json
  article.json
  cart.json
  search.json
  404.json
```

## index.json Example

```json
{
  "sections": {
    "hero": {
      "type": "hero",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Welcome to Our Store",
        "bg_color": "#000000"
      }
    },
    "featured-collection": {
      "type": "featured-collection",
      "settings": { "collection": "frontpage" }
    },
    "testimonials": {
      "type": "testimonials",
      "blocks": {
        "t1": { "type": "testimonial-card", "settings": { "quote": "Great!" } },
        "t2": { "type": "testimonial-card", "settings": { "quote": "Love it!" } }
      },
      "block_order": ["t1", "t2"]
    }
  },
  "order": ["hero", "featured-collection", "testimonials"]
}
```

`order` array controls section render sequence. Merchants drag-drop in customizer → JSON updates.

## Section Groups (header.json + footer.json)

```json
{
  "type": "header",
  "name": "Header",
  "sections": {
    "announcement": { "type": "announcement-bar", "settings": {} },
    "main-header": { "type": "header-main", "settings": {} }
  },
  "order": ["announcement", "main-header"]
}
```

Layout file references:
```liquid
{% sections 'header' %}
{{ content_for_layout }}
{% sections 'footer' %}
```

## product.json (PDP) Standard

```json
{
  "sections": {
    "main-product": { "type": "main-product" },
    "product-recommendations": { "type": "product-recommendations" },
    "trust-badges": { "type": "trust-badges" }
  },
  "order": ["main-product", "product-recommendations", "trust-badges"]
}
```

`main-product` section uses `{{ product }}` from URL context. Other sections render alongside.

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Never hardcode sections in template files (use JSON, not .liquid templates)
- ❌ Never skip `order` array (sections won't render)
- ❌ Never reference a section type that doesn't exist (build fails)
- ❌ Never define section groups for non-shared regions (use only for header/footer)

<!-- AUTHORING TODO: Capture template inventory per project type (single-product DTC, multi-collection brand, content-heavy editorial) after first 5 projects. -->

# Storefront GraphQL Query Patterns

**Owner:** conduit
**Purpose:** Author rate-limit-aware Storefront API queries for theme JS use.

## Authentication

Storefront API uses unauthenticated tokens (read-only public data). Token in `assets/theme.js`:

```js
const STOREFRONT_TOKEN = '{{ shop.permanent_domain }}'; // wrong
// Correct: inject via theme.liquid as JSON
window.SHOP = {
  storefrontToken: '{{ settings.storefront_api_token }}',  // settings_schema field
  domain: '{{ shop.permanent_domain }}'
};
```

## Endpoint

```
POST https://{shop}.myshopify.com/api/2025-01/graphql.json
```

## Rate Limits

- 1000 cost units / minute (rolling)
- Each query has a calculated cost (Shopify reports in response `extensions.cost`)
- Cost = sum of fields touched, with multipliers for connection sizes

## Query Cost Estimator (mandatory pre-flight)

```js
async function queryStorefront(query, variables) {
  const res = await fetch(`https://${SHOP.domain}/api/2025-01/graphql.json`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'X-Shopify-Storefront-Access-Token': SHOP.storefrontToken
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({ query, variables })
  });
  const json = await res.json();
  if (json.extensions?.cost?.actualQueryCost > 200) {
    console.warn('High-cost query detected', json.extensions.cost);
  }
  return json.data;
}
```

## Common Queries

### Product recommendations
```graphql
query ProductRecommendations($productId: ID!) {
  productRecommendations(productId: $productId) {
    id
    title
    handle
    featuredImage { url altText }
    priceRange { minVariantPrice { amount currencyCode } }
  }
}
```

### Customer login
```graphql
mutation CustomerAccessTokenCreate($input: CustomerAccessTokenCreateInput!) {
  customerAccessTokenCreate(input: $input) {
    customerAccessToken { accessToken expiresAt }
    customerUserErrors { field message code }
  }
}
```

### Predictive search (paginated)
```graphql
query Search($q: String!, $first: Int = 10) {
  predictiveSearch(query: $q, types: [PRODUCT], limit: $first) {
    products {
      id
      title
      handle
      featuredImage { url altText }
    }
  }
}
```

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Never call Storefront API from server-side code (it's a public token)
- ❌ Never query unbounded `products(first: 250)` — paginate with cursor
- ❌ Never request unused fields (cost cumulative)
- ❌ Never skip error handling on `userErrors[]` arrays
- ❌ Never store Storefront token in env vars (it IS public, but theme settings is fine)

<!-- AUTHORING TODO: Capture canonical queries after first 3 projects: cart, customer order history, product variants by SKU, collection metafields, blog filter. -->

# Admin API from Theme Bridge Patterns

**Owner:** conduit
**Purpose:** When a theme needs Admin API data (rare), use a server-side proxy. NEVER embed admin tokens in theme.

## When to Use Admin API from Theme

99% of theme use cases → Storefront API.

Admin API needed for:
- Custom data only available via Admin (e.g. inventory levels with full history)
- Webhook-triggered updates
- Customer Account API actions requiring admin scope

## Architecture

```
[Theme JS] →
  [Cloudflare Worker / Vercel Edge / Railway proxy] →
    [Shopify Admin GraphQL]
```

The proxy:
1. Receives request from theme JS (browser)
2. Validates request signature (HMAC + timestamp)
3. Adds Admin token from server env
4. Forwards to Shopify Admin GraphQL
5. Returns response to theme

Admin token NEVER touches theme files or browser.

## Proxy Code Pattern (Cloudflare Worker example)

```js
export default {
  async fetch(request, env) {
    if (request.method !== 'POST') return new Response('Method not allowed', { status: 405 });

    const body = await request.json();
    const sig = request.headers.get('x-boldteq-sig');

    // Verify HMAC
    const expectedSig = await hmacSHA256(JSON.stringify(body), env.SHARED_SECRET);
    if (sig !== expectedSig) return new Response('Forbidden', { status: 403 });

    // Forward to Shopify
    const shopifyRes = await fetch(`https://${env.SHOP_DOMAIN}/admin/api/2025-01/graphql.json`, {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        'X-Shopify-Access-Token': env.ADMIN_TOKEN
      },
      body: JSON.stringify(body)
    });
    return shopifyRes;
  }
};
```

## Theme JS Calling Pattern

```js
async function adminQuery(query, variables) {
  const body = JSON.stringify({ query, variables });
  const sig = await hmacSign(body, window.SHOP.proxySharedSecret); // public-safe key
  const res = await fetch('/api/admin-proxy', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'x-boldteq-sig': sig },
    body
  });
  return await res.json();
}
```

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ NEVER put Admin token in theme assets
- ❌ NEVER expose Admin token via window object
- ❌ NEVER skip HMAC verification on proxy
- ❌ NEVER use Admin API for customer-data fetches (use Customer Account API)
- ❌ NEVER cache admin responses without invalidation strategy

